a historical development.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:48.980
So for example, one of the
worries around the interpretation

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:55.030
of primitive accumulation
has to do with the the risk

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:58.610
of falling into the
theological philosophies

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:03.610
of history and therefore
have you over necessary

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.053
historical development.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:12.400
Another area that has to do

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:16.750
with the debates of primitive
accumulation has to do,

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:20.620
they're all of direct,
extra economic violence

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.110
within capitalist and
capitalist accumulation.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:27.680
And finally, obviously the the question

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:31.060
that absolutely controversial question

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:35.430
of the relationship between
gender racial oppression

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.580
and capitalism and
capitalism accumulation.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:44.220
Moreover depending on
what analysis we give

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.380
and what reading we give

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.763
of primitive accumulation, we also have,

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.830
we get different pictures of the way

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:54.610
in which capitalism works and the way

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.840
in which capitalism is distinct

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:59.950
or not distinct from
other modes of production.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:03.120
So is this is something that
is really specific peculiar

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.300
to capitalist is compared

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:08.893
to other modes of production
or forms of sociality.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.060
So, off course not address all

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.010
of these problems in one single lecture

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:21.620
But what I'm going to try
to do is to give first

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:24.720
a reading of primitive accumulation.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.240
So in other words, a general
overview or what happens

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.280
in this in Part VIII in
section eight of capital volume

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.030
one in the English edition.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.630
And then I will discuss the two main

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:40.110
lines of contemporary debates

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:44.430
and readings of primitive accumulation.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:49.430
The first one concerns
whether primitive accumulation

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:55.030
should be considered
as a fact of the past.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.070
So as the past of capitalism

00:08:58.203 --> 00:09:01.830
on whether we should that rather speak

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.800
of an ongoing primitive accumulation

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:09.800
that repeats constantly itself
within capitalist societies

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:13.270
the second debate concerns

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:16.470
what I already mentioned
that is the issue of violence

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:21.470
and race and their relation
to capitalist accumulation

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:24.010
and I know that some of the lectures

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:26.650
that proceeded me have already touched

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:29.010
upon this topic, especially
the role of slavery

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:34.010
and the transatlantic slay
market for for capitalism.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:41.370
So I will try to address also this debate.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:47.460
Okay, so let's start with
what our prints in Part VIII

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:50.057
of Capital Volume I

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:55.900
and also why Marx rights
Part VIII of Capital Volume I

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.983
on primitive accumulation.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:05.070
The first thing I want
to underline to stress

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:10.190
has to do with the fact
that the discussion

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:12.200
of primitive accumulation takes place

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.880
at the end of Volume I,
not at the beginning.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:19.880
So in other words, we do
have the marches on take

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:23.520
on historical processes
that led to the emergence

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:27.310
of capitalism in Europe, not
at the beginning of a capital

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:31.430
not as a prelude to capital,
but rather at the end.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:35.450
Now, why is this the case I take it

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:40.540
that it may have to do
with what Marx writes

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:45.540
in the (Mumbles) in terms
of how do read history.

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:51.860
In other words, it is
only after the neurologic

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.080
or capitalist accumulation
has been developed

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:58.800
has been expanded upon
and explained in its key

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:02.500
and most abstract aspects
that is possible to then

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:06.490
give a presentation of the
historical process that led

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.780
to the emergence of capitalism.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:10.210
So in other words, the key

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:13.503
for the interpretation of
the past is our present.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.460
So it is only in light
of our understanding

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:22.460
and analysis of the reality of
contemporary social relations

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:25.840
or production that we can
probably understand the serious

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:30.574
of seemingly disjoint historical process,

00:11:30.574 --> 00:11:32.740
historical events and historical facts

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:36.190
as actually a process
leading to an outcome.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:40.093
And the outcome is of
course our own reality.

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:44.490
So for this reason, I think,
or at least this is one

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:47.270
of the reasons I think why Part VIII

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:52.270
is at the end of Capital Volume I.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:56.370
So as you may have noticed

00:11:56.370 --> 00:12:00.890
I do think that Part VIII
has to do with the origin

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:04.460
the problem of the origin
and the emergence of capital.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:08.910
And that fully does fundamentally to do

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.490
with the problem or transition
I'm going to emphasize

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:16.780
and insist on this because
as I will explain later on

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:20.470
in a contemporary debates
about periods of accumulation

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:24.490
this element of transition is often lost

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:28.040
in attempts to basically
read primitive accumulation

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.763
as an ongoing process.

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:34.393
Now, what is Marx’s problem here?

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.640
He explains his problem

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:40.423
at the very beginning of the section.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:46.180
The problem is that throughout
Volume I Marx has shown

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:52.770
how capital is a self reproducing
model production governed

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:55.700
by its own inner logic

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.933
which is the logical
valorization of value.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:03.430
So once in existence,
capital basically constantly

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:08.172
posits itself as its own presupposition.

00:13:08.172 --> 00:13:10.430
So capital generates capital

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:14.570
through the exploitation of
labor power live in labor.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.130
And so it's expansion now

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:17.940
on an increased scale is the there mean

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:22.280
by the inner tendencies or capital itself.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.460
So let's say that in a sense

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:28.290
capital moves in a circuit
or with a circular motion

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:32.140
but of course, expanding at each circuit.

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:37.140
Now, if we take this to
be inner logical capital

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.470
so self-organizing value

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:44.430
and so on now we end up

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:46.850
with a problem, which is that this logic

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:50.450
cannot be used to explain
the emergence of capitalism.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:54.052
So in other words, if once
capital is in existence

00:13:54.052 --> 00:13:57.690
capital posits itself as
its own pursuit position

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:02.070
this cannot be true for
the historical emergence

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.140
of capital, because otherwise

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.883
we end up into circular reasoning.

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:13.430
So to summarize the problem
in the clearest possible terms

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:15.270
Marx needs to provide an account

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:17.120
of the emergence of capital.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:21.090
That first does not Eben
that ended up in sequel

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:24.460
or reasoning by setting
capital as the historical

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.750
original capital.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:31.950
And secondly, it needs to
also highlight the originality

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.770
peculiarity and specificity of capital

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:39.050
with regard to other modes of
production and forms of life

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:42.480
which also were based and
are based on exploitation

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.313
and domination.

00:14:43.313 --> 00:14:45.930
So what is it that makes
capitalism or capital

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:48.470
the kind of bloodthirsty
monster that it is

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:52.933
compared to other oppressive
modes of production.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:55.310
Now the first problem

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:56.540
which is a logical problem.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.210
So basically how to avoid the ending

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:01.640
up in an infinite regress
or circular reasoning

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:05.580
and so on was already
addressed by Adam Smith

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:10.250
in Wealth of Nations,
where Adam Smith postulated

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:12.000
that at the origin of capitalism

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.430
there must have been some
previous accumulation

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.343
of what he calls stocks
or stocks of capital.

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:21.733
However, Smith doesn't
really address this issue

00:15:21.733 --> 00:15:25.320
in historical terms, but
rather in logical ones.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:29.680
So in other words, it
is logical prerequisite

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:34.000
to avoid circular reasoning to postulate

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.020
a previous accumulation of stocks

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:42.160
but how these stocks were
accumulated is actually

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.997
not specified historically by Smith.

00:15:44.997 --> 00:15:48.960
And this allows Smith
to base, to offer a sort

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.170
of he didn't leak as Marx would say,

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:53.710
non-violent original myth.

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:58.120
I came to what Marx calls,
The Myth of the Original sin

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:59.440
of Adam and Eve.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:03.890
Now I'm going to share my screen hoping

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:06.190
that everything will work.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.333
Yeah. Okay.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:15.460
So here is the original
sin passage from Volume I.

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:23.080
This primitive accumulation
plays approximately

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.870
the same role in political
economy as original sin does

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:28.560
in theology.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:33.560
Adam bit the apple and thereupon
sin fell on the human race.

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:38.720
It's origin is supposed to
be explain when it is told

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:42.610
as an anecdote about
the past long, long ago

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.320
there were two sorts of people

