00:56:17.950 --> 00:56:22.360
In other words, it has (mumbles)

00:56:22.360 --> 00:56:25.493
of preserved, but in a
completely transparent way.

00:56:26.500 --> 00:56:31.060
So it is the case that the separation

00:56:31.060 --> 00:56:35.050
of workers from means of
production is not just the genesis

00:56:35.050 --> 00:56:37.900
but the constant requirement
to cut that is accumulation.

00:56:39.830 --> 00:56:43.540
And in this sense capital
accumulation does preserve

00:56:45.030 --> 00:56:48.050
this requirement from
primitive accumulation.

00:56:48.050 --> 00:56:53.050
So dispossession separation
from land and so on

00:56:53.690 --> 00:56:56.493
but he presents it in largely new forms.

00:56:57.700 --> 00:57:02.700
And to a large extent, this dispossession

00:57:02.950 --> 00:57:05.520
is the consequences of the very mechanism

00:57:05.520 --> 00:57:07.440
stock capital is the production.

00:57:07.440 --> 00:57:12.440
So the way in which wage works
in other cases, it is not

00:57:12.770 --> 00:57:17.130
it does require the intervention
of the state, but again

00:57:17.130 --> 00:57:19.460
it requires the intervention

00:57:19.460 --> 00:57:21.300
of an already capitalist state

00:57:21.300 --> 00:57:25.040
within a context in which
capitalism already exist

00:57:26.020 --> 00:57:30.550
and this is the fundamental
difference with the processes

00:57:30.550 --> 00:57:31.923
Of primitive accumulation.

00:57:33.600 --> 00:57:38.320
So the fundamental
difference, just to sum up

00:57:39.530 --> 00:57:42.490
between the primitive
accumulation described

00:57:42.490 --> 00:57:45.160
in Capital Volume I and processes

00:57:45.160 --> 00:57:48.310
of expropriation taking place
within a capitalist society

00:57:48.310 --> 00:57:52.000
is that these processes are a consequence

00:57:52.000 --> 00:57:54.180
of what Marx calls the human laws

00:57:54.180 --> 00:57:56.460
of capitalist production itself

00:57:56.460 --> 00:57:58.804
through the centuries national capitals.

00:57:58.804 --> 00:58:02.120
I want to add here that at least

00:58:02.120 --> 00:58:05.090
in my own take these human laws

00:58:05.090 --> 00:58:09.400
in order to be realized often
do require the intervention

00:58:09.400 --> 00:58:14.400
of the state and also extra
economic compulsion and so on.

00:58:15.130 --> 00:58:17.320
But again, as a consequence

00:58:17.320 --> 00:58:21.360
of the drive to accumulate
the capitalist drive

00:58:21.360 --> 00:58:23.350
to valorization of value

00:58:24.570 --> 00:58:26.980
while as I have already
mentioned, the processes

00:58:26.980 --> 00:58:31.210
of primitive accumulation
described in a Volume I are not

00:58:31.210 --> 00:58:35.040
and cannot be the consequence of the logic

00:58:35.040 --> 00:58:38.643
or in human laws of capitalist production.

00:58:40.190 --> 00:58:45.190
Now, one may think that this
is a bit of philological

00:58:46.530 --> 00:58:49.648
matter, or like, or maybe
a (muffled speaking)

00:58:49.648 --> 00:58:52.140
So in other words, and it's
true that I'm a bit narrow.

00:58:52.140 --> 00:58:56.010
So I like conceptual
qualifications and distinctions.

00:58:56.010 --> 00:59:00.480
And I don't like maybe
because, I come from philosophy

00:59:00.480 --> 00:59:04.260
so I like concepts to do the
